#. Tag: title
#: webbrowse.docbook:6
#, no-c-format
msgid "Webbrowsing with &konqueror;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&konqueror; is &kde;'s open source, standards compliant webbrowser. It's "
"home page is <ulink url=\"http://www.konqueror.org\">http://www.konqueror."
"org</ulink> where a &konqueror; specific <acronym>FAQ</acronym> can be found."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where does the name &konqueror; come from?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It's a word play on the other browsers' names. After the Navigator and the "
"Explorer comes the Conqueror; it's spelled with a K to show that it's part "
"of &kde;. The name change also moves away from <quote>kfm</quote> (the &kde; "
"file manager, &konqueror;'s predecessor) which represented only file "
"management."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "Can I run &konqueror; without running &kde;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes. Just install &Qt;, kdelibs and kdebase, and from your favorite window "
"manager just launch &konqueror;. It should work just fine, but if it doesn't "
"(&kde; developers don't test that case often), report it to http://bugs.kde."
"org and try running \"kdeinit\" before running &konqueror;, it usually "
"helps. This is of course the same for any other &kde; application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Why doesn't &konqueror; show the contents of an image's <sgmltag class="
"\"attribute\">ALT</sgmltag> attribute in a tooltip?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is no standard that states the <sgmltag class=\"attribute\">ALT</"
"sgmltag> attribute should appear as a tooltip. The specification calls for "
"<sgmltag class=\"attribute\">ALT</sgmltag> to be displayed in place of the "
"image, as in text-mode only browsers such at lynx or w3m. Abusing the "
"<sgmltag class=\"attribute\">ALT</sgmltag> attribute is bad for "
"accessibility. Tooltips are supposed to come from the <sgmltag class="
"\"attribute\">TITLE</sgmltag> attribute and this is implemented in "
"&konqueror;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I use &konqueror; as a web browser with a proxy?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&konqueror; can be used with &HTTP; and &FTP; proxies. To set up the proxy "
"server in &konqueror;, just select <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guisubmenu>Configure &konqueror;...</guisubmenu></menuchoice> from "
"the &konqueror; menu and go to the <guilabel>Proxy</guilabel> tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I import bookmarks from another browser into &konqueror; ?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To import bookmarks from another browser into &konqueror; select "
"<guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu><guimenuitem>Edit Bookmarks</guimenuitem> and "
"then in the <application>Bookmark Editor</application> select <guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Import</guimenuitem>. Then select the browser you would "
"like to import bookmarks from. In the Open dialog, navigate to the location "
"of the folder or file your bookmarks are contained in and click "
"<guilabel>Open</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How can I make &konqueror; only show certain bookmarks in the bookmarks "
"toolbar?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &konqueror; go to <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &konqueror;...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. "
"Then select <guilabel>Web Behaviour</guilabel> from the icon list. Under the "
"<guilabel>Bookmarks</guilabel> heading, place a check in the box next to "
"<guilabel>Show only marked bookmarks in bookmark toolbar</guilabel>. Now in "
"the <application>Bookmark Editor</application> an option to <guilabel>Show "
"in Toolbar</guilabel> appears on clicking with the &RMB; on any bookmark "
"entry or in the <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> menu when the entry is highlighted. "
"Folders can also be shown in the bookmarks toolbar in much the same way."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"How do I fool a site into believing &konqueror; is &Netscape; or some other "
"browser?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &konqueror;, select <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Konqueror...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and "
"in the configuration dialog, select <guilabel>Browser Identification</"
"guilabel>. Default and site-specific browser identifications can be set from "
"here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&konqueror; is taking a really long time to load webpages, what could cause "
"this?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Quite often &konqueror; loading webpages slowly is caused by <acronym>DNS</"
"acronym> servers with broken <acronym>IPV6</acronym> support. Adding the "
"following to <filename>/etc/profile</filename> or any other script that is "
"sourced on login should solve this problem: <screen>\n"
"export KDE_NO_IPV6=true\n"
"</screen> for bourne compatible shells, and for C-style shells:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: webbrowse.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "setenv KDE_NO_IPV6 true"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I configure &konqueror; to run &Java; applets?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"&konqueror;...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from &konqueror;'s menubar and "
"then select <guilabel>Java &amp; Javascript</guilabel>. Set the "
"<guilabel>Path to Java executable</guilabel> correctly. If it doesn't work, "
"please check the <ulink url=\"http://www.konqueror.org/javahowto/"
"\">Konqueror + Java HOWTO</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "How do I block unrequested popup windows in &konqueror;?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&konqueror; has a new 'smart' policy for JavaScript popups. From the "
"&konqueror; main window, select <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure &konqueror;...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and then "
"<guilabel>Java &amp; JavaScript</guilabel>. On the <guilabel>JavaScript</"
"guilabel> tab, under <guilabel>Global JavaScript Policies</guilabel> set the "
"radio button beside <guilabel>Open new windows:</guilabel> to "
"<guilabel>Smart</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Why doesn't my banking site work with &konqueror;? It pops up a new window "
"with the login screen in other browsers, but not in &konqueror;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Make sure you have Javascript enabled, and the default JavaScript web popups "
"policy set to <guilabel>Ask</guilabel> or <guilabel>Allow</guilabel>. The "
"<guilabel>Smart</guilabel> policy is not always sufficient for some banks. "
"Many banks also require &Java; support. You can find more help on enabling "
"this at <ulink url=\"http://www.konqueror.org/\">http://www.konqueror.org/</"
"ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Can &konqueror; use user-specified stylesheets, like those in the Firefox "
"adblock extention?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Yes, you can set &konqueror; to use any kind of valid <acronym>css</acronym> "
"stylesheet to filter webcontent or improve accessibility. From the "
"&konqueror; main window simply click <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure &konqueror;...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and select "
"<guilabel>Stylesheets</guilabel>. Set the radio button to <guilabel>Use user-"
"defined stylesheet</guilabel> and browse to where the stylesheet you want to "
"use is located. Alternatively, you can select <guilabel>Use accessibility "
"stylesheet defined in \"Customize\" tab</guilabel> and then set your own "
"options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An example of <acronym>css</acronym> rules that implement ad blocking can be "
"found at: <ulink url=\"http://www.mozilla.org/support/firefox/adblock\"> "
"http://www.mozilla.org/support/firefox/adblock</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Why does &konqueror; display a plain grey square when I try to view flash "
"animations, even though the flash plugin is installed?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Under the latest versions of X.org, having the composite extension loaded "
"can cause problems with the flash plugin. Try disabling the composite "
"extension and see if normal flash operation is restored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "Why can't &konqueror; render &GIF; images?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is because you did not enable &GIF; support in &Qt;. Please see <xref "
"linkend=\"gif\"/> for more details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When I try to open a web page with &konqueror;, I get the message: "
"<quote>There appears to be a configuration error. You have associated "
"Konqueror with text/html, but it cannot handle this file type.</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You need to make sure that the embedding settings for the text/html "
"<acronym>MIME</acronym> type are correct:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &konqueror;, go to <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &konqueror;...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and "
"then to the <guilabel>File Associations</guilabel> page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open text->html in the tree view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: webbrowse.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the <guilabel>Embedding</guilabel> tab. Make sure that "
"<guilabel>Left Click Action</guilabel> is set to <guilabel>Show file in "
"embedded viewer</guilabel>, and that <guilabel>KHTML (khtml)</guilabel> is "
"at the top of <guilabel>Services Preference Order</guilabel>."
msgstr ""
